# Employee Attrition Analysis – Python

## Overview

An employee attrition analysis project using Python and Pandas to explore employee records, clean the data, analyze attrition patterns, and identify workforce retention insights.

## Business Problem

Analyze employee data to understand attrition patterns across departments, gender, age, job satisfaction, overtime, and salary levels.

## Tools & Technologies

- Python
- Pandas
- Matplotlib
- Data Analysis
- Data Cleaning
- Data Visualization

## Data Preparation

- Loaded and explored employee data
- Detected null values
- Removed duplicate records
- Corrected incorrect data
- Prepared the dataset for analysis

## Analysis

Used Pandas Series, DataFrame operations, and GroupBy aggregations to analyze employee attrition patterns.

## Visualizations

Created:

- Bar Charts
- Pie Charts
- Histograms

## Key Insights

- Employees working overtime showed higher attrition risk
- Employees with low job satisfaction showed higher attrition risk
- Employees with salaries below 40,000 showed higher attrition risk
- Analyzed attrition patterns across 6 departments
- Examined attrition patterns by gender and age distribution
